Copyright the office-word-diff authors (https://github.com/yuch85)

The files diff-wordmode.js, token-map.js, sentence-diff.js, block-replace.js
and the computeDiff function in index.js were vendored from:

  https://github.com/yuch85/office-word-diff
  commit 81315f2fae23ba8cf9f40c13bdfd17d0e444d137

licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0 (see LICENSE in this
directory). The pinned source identifies the inherited implementation;
local adaptations must be maintained and reviewed separately.

Inherited machinery includes regex token encoding, diff-match-patch
computation and decoding, computeDiff, token/range mapping, batched Word
searches, tracked application, and token-to-sentence-to-block fallbacks.
The upstream README already demonstrates applyAISuggestion(aiGeneratedText)
with GPT/Claude-generated text and preview statistics; it does not supply
a model client or proposal-management system.

Modifications relative to the pinned upstream source:
- Files renamed to kebab-case and imports adjusted; unused OfficeWordDiff,
  applyWordDiff, getDiffStats and logger utilities were not vendored.
- token-map.js computes client-side token positions and selects needed
  anchors, deduplicates searches, assigns greedy substring occurrence
  indices within coarse ranges (including embedded matches), and coalesces
  deletion spans.
- sentence-diff.js preserves repeated sentence occurrences, counts sentences
  per diff chunk, and handles single-sentence and all-deleted fallbacks.
- Application strategies accept options.trackChanges and use finally-based
  cleanup. These changes do not provide atomic application or restoration
  of arbitrary prior document or tracking state.

char-diff.js has no counterpart at the pinned upstream revision. It adds a
CJK Word adapter using existing diff-match-patch diff_main and diff_cleanupMerge,
with script detection, occurrence-indexed spans and insertion anchors,
surrogate-safe search pieces, cursor fallback, reverse application, and an
operation cap. It is not a new character-diff algorithm. Claric's proposal
lifecycle, endpoint clients, document orchestration and structured-tool
integration are separate additions relative to this pinned source.
